# SSS-PROFILE p4: the screen pass - a skin profile scatters light on screen. Test object = CONTRACT §9 Q7: the
# Lee Perry-Smith head scan (CC BY 3.0, Infinite-Realities; docs licence record) in Projects/Desert/Content/Meshes/Test,
# material M_Skin_SSS (SubsurfaceProfileSurface, profile Materials/Subsurface/Skin.dsssprofile = UE skin defaults),
# put on Starter's Metal_40 sphere entity; the sun turned to light it from the side.
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано properties 106508827693059193
Дано set 106508827693059193 StaticMeshData.MeshHandle assets:Meshes/Test/LeePerrySmith.glb
Дано set 106508827693059193 StaticMeshData.MaterialSlots.0 assets:Materials/M_Skin_SSS.demat
Дано run Entity Metal_40
Дано --subject selection set Scale 3,3,3
Дано run Entity Sun
Дано --subject selection set Translation -100,-25,-10
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -70,60,-395
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,0,-1
Когда set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.SubsurfaceScattering true
Тогда-вид 1_skin_on soft red-tinted light bleed at the terminator and around nose/ears; specular highlights stay sharp
Когда set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.SubsurfaceScattering false
Тогда-вид 2_skin_off same view, hard Lambert terminator, no other change
Когда set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.SubsurfaceScattering true
Когда set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.SubsurfaceScale 4
Тогда-вид 3_scale4 wider bleed, no haloes onto the background, no banding
